<title>UK: British Steel dips as Kleinwort downgrades.</title>
<headline>British Steel dips as Kleinwort downgrades.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British Steel Plc fell to a three-month low on Wednesday as analysts at Kleinwort Benson cut the stock to a &quot;hold&quot; from a &quot;buy,&quot; market sources said.</p>
<p>The stock was down 1-1/2p at 171 by 0852 GMT, after reaching a day's low of 170-1/2 -- its lowest since July 24.  </p>
<p>Analysts at the brokerage were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 5106</p>
